Based on the standard kit picture here is the list adapted to our farm scenario:
-Sensors & Input Modules (From Kit) :
* Sensor Module (Microphone): Detects flock distress or panic noise spikes.
* Photoresistor (LDR / Light Sensor): Monitors day/night lighting cycles in the poultry hall.
* Potentiometer: Manual threshold tuning or simulated gas/temperature level adjustment.
* Keypad (4x4 Matrix) / Push Buttons: Control room interface for manual overrides and system authorization PINs.
* IR Receiver + Remote Controller: Local manual controls or simulated wireless management.
-Actuators & Output Modules (From Kit) :
* DC Motor with Fan Blade (if we have Relay/Driver): Ventilation fan to simulate hall cooling or gas extraction (central to the rejected spoofed "fans off" cyber demo).
* 5V Single-Channel Relay Module: Switches the ventilation motor, heating element, or drinker pump.
* Active/Passive Buzzer: Acoustic alarm for system faults, critical levels, or security breaches.
* Discrete LEDs (Red, Green, Yellow, Blue): Visual indicators for normal operation, critical warnings, and cyber-attack alerts.
* 16x2 I2C LCD Display: Displays live telemetry (water levels, ambient status, and cyber attack rejection logs).
* Stepper Motor / Small Geared Motor: Automated feed dispenser valve or mechanical window vent opener.
